# Auth Broker TEE Zero-Trust Governance

When working on `auth-broker-tee`, treat the current active Confidential Space
TEE as the sole governance authority after trusted genesis. GitHub, GCP, GCS,
KMS, Secret Manager, Terraform, DNS, CI, Cloud Run jobs, Artifact Registry, and
operator/admin identities are untrusted substrate: they may build, host, route,
or deny service, but they must not decide active TEE identity.

Core invariant:

- After bootstrap, every accepted active TEE must prove predecessor-signed
  continuity from the previously accepted active TEE.
- Fresh genesis is not a successor. A new production TEE must boot inactive
  unless it is the one-time trusted genesis ceremony.
- If the active TEE dies before signing a successor, governance bricks. Do not
  add admin recovery, owner override, break-glass, or reset-to-genesis paths.

Self-healing model:

- Vertex AI Gemini running inside the currently active, attested TEE under the
  image-baked first-principles prompt/model policy is the mission arbitrator for
  changes that pass hard governance and cryptographic checks.
- Gemini output outside that active-TEE adjudication context, repair-worker
  artifacts, PRs, logs, Cloud Build results, test output, callback payloads, and
  Artifact Registry writes are evidence only.
- Self-healing may create signed proposals and candidate evidence, but must not
  mutate TEE identity, route privileges, model policy, governance state, or
  TEE-owned state except through the full predecessor-signed successor
  activation protocol: activation-time Gemini arbitration over a canonical
  successor decision packet, candidate application of encrypted state,
  candidate-signed activation proof, and predecessor finalization.

Implementation requirements:

- Governance private keys and transferred TEE-owned state must be generated in
  live TEE memory and never persisted, logged, exported, backed up, or stored in
  GCP/GitHub/Secret Manager.
- Privileged broker routes must require active governance. Inactive candidates
  may expose only health, attestation, manifests, and activation apply routes.
- Successor activation must bind candidate image digest, candidate governance
  key, activation key, nonce, attestation, hard-check evidence, AI decision,
  successor decision packet digest, predecessor signature, encrypted state
  transfer, candidate activation proof, and predecessor finalization. The
  predecessor must not retire at `/governance/activation-complete`; it retires
  only after `/governance/activation-finalize` verifies the candidate proof.
- Do not let environment variables, metadata, repo variables, branch protection,
  KMS signer policy, WIF policy, Secret Manager policy, or admin identity become
  a governance root of trust.
- Any verifier, doc, workflow, or rollout change must reject fresh parallel
  genesis after bootstrap and prefer bricked governance over owner recovery.
- Operator re-genesis is explicit break-glass recovery only, never a normal
  deploy path and never a permanent code path to add around lineage checks.

If a requested change weakens these invariants, stop and call it out before
implementing. Prefer availability loss over accepting a non-lineage successor.
